      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Subtitles for any video\n\n1. Load a video with speech in **Video with speech**.\n2. Run. Whisper large-v3 writes down what is said and times every word, and Word Timestamps to Subtitles groups the words into subtitle lines.\n\nOutputs: an .srt file in `output/subtitles/`, a copy of the video with the subtitles burned in, in `output/video/`, and the plain transcript in the **Transcript** box. Burned-in subtitles draw Latin, Greek and Cyrillic letters; for other scripts use the .srt.\n\nThe language is detected; when it comes out wrong, set it in the speech to text node. Whisper knows 100 languages and times words in all of them. For Finnish it is the one to use: in the [BuzzASR](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.09554) comparison it transcribed Finnish with 1.89 % character errors. `max_characters` and `max_seconds` decide how long one subtitle line gets."
      ],
      "title": "How to use"
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        960,
        720
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## About this workflow\n\nBuilt for this repo. Whisper Speech to Text, Word Timestamps to Subtitles, Burn In Subtitles and Save Subtitles are this repo's template pack nodes; the first runs OpenAI's Whisper large-v3 (Apache-2.0) through Hugging Face transformers.\n\nSample clip `dubit_input.mp4` from Lightricks' ComfyUI-LTXVideo examples.\n\nAsset profile: `whisper-subtitles`."
      ],
      "title": "About this workflow"
    }
